    {
      "abstract": "This study proposes a stochastic model predictive control (SMPC) strategy with wave preview for collective blade pitch control of the 10 MW LIFES50+ OO-Star semi-submersible floating offshore wind turbine under above-rated wind conditions. Wind disturbances are modeled probabilistically using a tube-based approach, avoiding the need for explicit wind preview, while wave excitation force is incorporated as a deterministic previewed input. This decoupling allows the prediction horizon to be selected based primarily on wave dynamics, thereby simplifying control design considerations.Simulation results indicate that the proposed control strategy improves rotor speed regulation, mitigates platform pitch and tower-top acceleration, and reduces structural loads at the tower base, fairlead, and blade root. Electrical power overshoot is slightly reduced, with minimal impact on mean power and fluctuations. Sensitivity analysis shows that the required wave preview horizon depends on model dynamics and optimization feasibility, with approximately 0.5 s sufficient to achieve performance gains.",
